 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to a license\nto sell liquor at retail for consumption on certain premises",
    "basePrintNo": "S3534",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3534-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §64, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S3534\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to a\nlicense to sell liquor at retail for consumption on certain premises\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe bill creates an exception to the Alcoholic Beverage Control Law,\nallowing a license to be issued to a location currently too close to a\nhouse of worship. The license application has the support of that house\nof worship.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends subdivision 7 of section 64 of the Alcoholic Beverage\nControl Law by adding a new paragraph (e-15).\n\nSection 2: Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Alcoholic Beverage Control law prohibits the sale for on-premises\nconsumption of alcohol at any location within 200 feet of a building\noccupied exclusively as a house of worship. This legislation will allow\nthe State Liquor Authority to issue a license to a location.  Other\nexceptions have been made for similar establishments where the nearby\nhouse of worship is in support of the application. In this case, the\nestablishment has the support of the adjacent house of worship.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
